# uploaded images — see README. Deliberately not committed: the photography
# includes minors whose written parental consent is not held, and this repo is
# public. Back the folder up with the rest of the deploy, not with git.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, `uploads/` also matched
# src/routes/uploads/, which is the route that *serves* the folder — so a fresh
# clone had the images ignored and no code to serve them either.
/uploads/

# Photography and video: large, and the photography includes minors whose
# written parental consent is not held. Drop them in locally; do not commit.
static/assets/img/
static/assets/video/
